      "content": "it's just hard to look at the \"logic\" of staying when everything feels so heavy and empty. people talk about \"resilience\" or \"finding purpose\" like it's some mandatory requirement, but if the universe is truly indifferent, then isn't the choice to leave just as valid as the choice to stay? like, if autonomy is the highest value, shouldn't we have the right to decide when the loop is finished?",
